BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260711T180000Z
DTEND:20260711T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260711T000000Z
SUMMARY:FREE CONCERT: Celebrating America with Florian Schantz Jazz Combo
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate America's 250th Birthday with the Florian Schantz 
 Jazz Combo at the Bloomfield Library on Saturday\, July 11\, 2026\, at 
 2PM.\n\nKnown for their engaging historical music programs\, the Florian 
 Schantz Jazz Combo will present a spirited musical journey through 
 patriotic songs spanning America's 250-year history. Combining live 
 performance with entertaining narration\, the ensemble explores the stories 
 behind the music\, composers\, musicians\, instruments\, and musical styles 
 that have helped shape the nation's cultural heritage.\n\nLed by 
 24-year-old professional trumpeter Florian Schantz\, the group has 
 performed nearly 1\,100 engagements throughout New Jersey\, New York\, 
 Connecticut\, Pennsylvania\, and Germany. Their appearances have included 
 more than 200 libraries\, as well as museums\, historical societies\, 
 schools\, senior centers\, community celebrations\, and private events. 
 More about the band at www.VFSJazz.com
LOCATION:Bloomfield - Theater\, Bloomfield Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Bloomfield Library":MAILTO:reference@bloomfield.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Performance
UID:LibCal-10270-17032507
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17032507
END:VEVENT
